nodecode-tab-watchdog is a rewrite of web3blind's web3blind/hermes-chrome-tab-watchdog:

  https://github.com/web3blind/hermes-chrome-tab-watchdog
  commit 15b873f13df8275c59a18cbe4a9a2ec71266af50
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 web3blind (LICENSE)

The rewrite keeps the original's judgement of a stale tab -- a blank page left for blank_minutes,
a second copy of a url left for duplicate_hours, a tab nothing has touched for idle_hours -- its
bound of five closes a sweep, its refusal to close the last page, its keeping of one blank tab,
its second look before closing and its check that each one is gone, and its settings, renamed to
the config section's spelling. What it does not do is the original's plumbing, because Nodecode
has no counterpart for it: the loopback CDP proxy every browser tool was routed through, the
observer WebSocket session with its focus script, the per-call leases that proxy enabled, the
SQLite ledger (a small JSON file under the home takes its place), and the native cron entry
point, which is now a worker the cell starts when `auto` is on. The source is Common Lisp written
for Nodecode's cell contract, with none of the original's Python, so a reader who compares them
should compare the rules, not the files.
